<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Majorca</h1><p class="st-meta">1231 CE – 1715 CE · capital Palma</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Christian kingdom created after James I's conquest of Majorca, independent under its own dynasty from 1276 to 1344 and a realm of Aragon thereafter.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> in 1229, then <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ebusus">Ibiza</a> in 1235, and established a separate kingdom. On his death in 1276 he left Majorca, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-montpellier">Montpellier</a> to his younger son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-majorca">James II</a>, creating an independent dynasty.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> trading state, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palma">Palma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perpignan">Perpignan</a> as royal seats, merchant fleets reaching <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and a famed school of cartographers who made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-atlas">Catalan Atlas</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-llull">Ramon Llull</a>, philosopher and missionary, was its most famous son. Its kings were forced to accept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassalage</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-iv-of-aragon">Peter IV of Aragon</a> seized the kingdom in 1343-1344, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-iii-of-majorca">James III</a> was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-llucmajor">Llucmajor</a> in 1349 trying to retake it. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> remained a separate realm within the Crown until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nueva-planta-decrees">Nueva Planta</a> decree of 1715.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-majorca.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Majorca" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: HansenBCN · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandera_del_Reino_de_Mallorca.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1231 CE – 1715 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Palma</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>James I, James II of Majorca, James III of Majorca</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Catalan, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Regne de Mallorca, Kingdom of Mallorca</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1473&amp;focus=kingdom-of-majorca" aria-label="Kingdom of Majorca on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4745 761 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Majorca lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5065 1017L5093 888M5065 1017L4794 1282M5065 1017L4984 945M5065 1017L4909 989M5065 1017L5070 916"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5093 888h0M4794 1282h0M4984 945h0M4909 989h0M5070 916h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5065 1017h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5065 1017h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Palma. <a href="/atlas?year=1473&amp;focus=kingdom-of-majorca">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
